<tei:p><tei:pb n="750" ed="1949 lifecycle" facs="https://archive.org/download/PhilipBirnbaumHaSiddurHaShalemTheDailyPrayerBook1949/page/n774_medium.jpg"/><tei:milestone unit="prayer-part" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:lifecycle/text/pidyon_present"/>This is my first-born son, the first-born of his mother. The Holy One, blessed be he, has commanded to redeem him, as it is said: <tei:seg source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:numbers/18/16"><tei:milestone unit="quotation" corresp="urn:x-opensiddur:text:siddur:lifecycle/text/pidyon_present/shekel_hakodesh"/>“The redemption-price for each first-born son of the age of one month shall be fixed at five sacred silver shekels at the rate of twenty gerahs.” <tei:milestone unit="quotation"/></tei:seg>And it is said: <tei:seg source="urn:x-opensiddur:text:bible:exodus/13/2">“Consecrate every first-born to me, whatever is first-born in Israel, of man or beast, since it belongs to me.”</tei:seg><tei:milestone unit="prayer-part"/></tei:p>
    </tei:body>
